<title>NORWAY: Kvaerner wins NOK 170 mln Asian deals.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner wins NOK 170 mln Asian deals.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-Norwegian construction and engineering group Kvaerner ASA said on Monday had won two contracts in Asia worth a total of 170 million crowns.</p>
<p>The company said its German pulp and paper unit, Kvaerner Panel Systems, would deliver a plant for continuous fibre board worth 110 million crowns to an unnamed customer in Xinglong, Heilongjiang province in China.</p>
<p>Kvaerner Panel also has won a 60 million crowns deal with Jayakuik Snd Bhd of Malaysia for the installation of a particle board plant.</p>
<p>The contract includes the main machinery, control system, environmental protection equipment and the complete plant engineering.</p>
<p>--Tanya Pang, Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
